Think of AKS security as 5 layers:
1. Identity & Access
2. Network Security
3. Cluster Security
4. Workload Security
5. Data & Secrets Security


🧠 1. Identity & Access (MOST IMPORTANT)
✅ Key Topics

Azure AD Integration with AKS
Azure RBAC vs Kubernetes RBAC
Managed Identities (System/User Assigned)
Workload Identity (replacement for Pod Identity)
Service Accounts & RBAC bindings

You should know:

Difference:
Azure RBAC → controls who accesses cluster
Kubernetes RBAC → controls what they do inside cluster


How pods access Azure resources securely:
Pod → Service Account → OIDC → Managed Identity

🌐 2. Network Security (CRITICAL IN PRODUCTION)
✅ Key Topics

Azure CNI vs Kubenet security implications
Network Policies (Azure / Calico)
NSGs (Network Security Groups)
Private AKS Cluster
API Server Authorized IP Ranges
Azure Firewall / WAF integration


🔥 Real Expectations
You should design:
✅ Private cluster:
Terraformprivate_cluster_enabled = trueShow more lines
✅ Restrict API access:
Terraformapi_server_authorized_ip_ranges = ["YourIP"]Show more lines
✅ Pod-level communication control:
YAMLNetworkPolicyShow more lines

⚡ Real Scenario
👉 Prevent:
frontend → talking to DB directly


🛡️ 3. Cluster Hardening
✅ Key Topics

Disable local accounts
Azure Policy for AKS
Defender for Containers
CIS AKS Benchmark
Pod Security Standards (restricted/baseline)


🔥 Production Practices
✅ Disable basic auth:
Terraformlocal_account_disabled = trueShow more lines
✅ Enforce security via Azure Policy:
No privileged containers
Only approved images


⚡ Real Scenario
👉 Block deployments with:
privileged: true
hostPath volumes


📦 4. Workload Security
✅ Key Topics

Pod Security Context
Admission Controllers
Image scanning (ACR + Defender)
Runtime security (Falco / Defender)


🔥 Example (Security Context)
YAMLsecurityContext:  runAsNonRoot: true  
readOnlyRootFilesystem: trueShow 

✅ Image Security
Scan images in ACR
Block vulnerable images

⚡ Real Incident
👉 Old vulnerable image deployed → exploited → crypto mining attack


🔐 5. Secrets & Data Security
✅ Key Topics

Azure Key Vault integration
CSI Secret Store Driver
Encryption at rest (etcd managed)
TLS & certificates


🔥 Best Practice
✅ NEVER store secrets in YAML:
YAML# BAD PRACTICEenv:  password: admin123Show more lines
✅ Use Key Vault:
